%description:

RFC 9293 section 3.8.6.1, SHLD-29 — a zero window that comes while the override timer runs gets its first probe one RTO later.

The rule: "The transmitting host SHOULD send the first zero-window probe when a zero window has existed for the
retransmission timeout period (SHLD-29)". The sender SWS avoidance of section 3.8.6.2.1 holds data with the override
timer, which is the persist timer in the role of the override. When the window closes while that timer runs, the timer
must time the first probe from the moment the window closed, not keep the time that is left of the override. The
reviewer document is ../sws-override-timer.md.

Host under test: host1, with an MSS of 1000 bytes and a minimum RTO of 2 s, so its RTO is 2 s, sends 5000 bytes. The
TS option takes 12 bytes of each segment, so a full segment holds 988 bytes. Peer: host2, with an advertised window of
3464 bytes, reads nothing. After three segments, 2964 bytes, the window of host2 is 500 bytes, and host1 holds the
rest from about 0.2 s. At 0.5 s host2 sends 100 bytes, and the tap sets the window of that segment to 0, as a peer that
shrinks its window does.

Observation: host1 sends no data and no probe for 1.9 s after the window closed, and sends its first probe one RTO,
2 s, after it. A timer that keeps the time of the override sends the probe at about 1.2 s, 0.7 s after the window
closed.

Expected result: PASS.

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("Rfc9293SwsOverrideZeroWindow")
        .act(action().at(0.0).run<TcpTestApp>("host2.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) {
            app.socket().setAutoRead(false);
            app.socket().bind(1000);
            app.socket().listen();
        }))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.ackBit == true && tcp.window == 500")
             .describe("the ACK of host2 that leaves a window of 500 bytes: host1 holds its data")
             .within(1.0))
        .meanwhile(tap("tap").from("host2").filterPacket("tcp.pshBit == true").nth(1).set("tcp.window", "0")
                       .describe("the data segment of host2: the window field 0"))
        .act(action().at(0.5).run<TcpTestApp>("host2.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) {
            app.sendData(app.accepted(0), 100);
        }))
        .never(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
              .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
              .describe("data or a probe before one RTO after the window closed")
              .within(1.9))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
             .describe("the first zero-window probe, one RTO after the window closed")
             .within(0.2));
}

%activity:
EV << "Rfc9293SwsOverrideZeroWindow compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
**.tcp.mss = 1000
*.host1.tcp.minRexmitTimeout = 2s
*.host2.tcp.advertisedWindow = 3464
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 5000B
*.host2.app[0].typename = "TcpTestApp"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST Rfc9293SwsOverrideZeroWindow: PASS
